  "description": "<div>\n  <p>Each ticket is a directed flight <code>[departure, arrival]</code>. Starting at <code>JFK</code>, arrange a route that uses every ticket exactly once; duplicate tickets are separate flights. Return the visited airports in travel order. If no route can use all tickets from JFK, return an empty array.</p>\n  <p>There can be several complete routes. Return the <strong>lexicographically smallest airport sequence</strong>, comparing the sequences from left to right by their airport codes. With no tickets, the route is <code>[\"JFK\"]</code>.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> tickets = [[&quot;JFK&quot;,&quot;SFO&quot;],[&quot;JFK&quot;,&quot;ATL&quot;],[&quot;SFO&quot;,&quot;ATL&quot;],[&quot;ATL&quot;,&quot;JFK&quot;],[&quot;ATL&quot;,&quot;SFO&quot;]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [&quot;JFK&quot;,&quot;ATL&quot;,&quot;JFK&quot;,&quot;SFO&quot;,&quot;ATL&quot;,&quot;SFO&quot;]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> ATL is the smaller viable next airport and the route uses all five tickets.</pre>\n\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> tickets = [[&quot;JFK&quot;,&quot;KUL&quot;],[&quot;JFK&quot;,&quot;NRT&quot;],[&quot;NRT&quot;,&quot;JFK&quot;]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [&quot;JFK&quot;,&quot;NRT&quot;,&quot;JFK&quot;,&quot;KUL&quot;]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Going to KUL first strands the other tickets, so NRT must come first.</pre>\n\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> tickets = [[&quot;SFO&quot;,&quot;ATL&quot;]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> []\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> There is no way to leave JFK and use the ticket.</pre>\n\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= tickets.length &lt;= 100</code>.</li>\n    <li>Every airport code is exactly three uppercase English letters. The route always starts at <code>JFK</code>; tickets may repeat.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
